# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Virtual environment
#
# NOTE: this project has its own top-level Lib/ and Scripts/ directories that
# hold source code. A virtualenv also contains Lib/ and Scripts/, so NEVER add
# bare "Lib/" or "Scripts/" patterns here - they would silently exclude the
# entire codebase. Exclude the venv by its own directory name only.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.venv/
venv/
env/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Python bytecode / build artefacts
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.so
build/
dist/
*.egg-info/
.eggs/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Tooling caches
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Editor / IDE
#
# .vscode/settings.json IS tracked on purpose: it points Pylance at Lib/ so
# imports resolve, and selects the .venv interpreter. Without it every script
# shows false "could not be resolved" warnings.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.vscode/*
!.vscode/settings.json
.idea/
*.swp
*~

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OS clutter
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
Thumbs.db
ehthumbs.db
Desktop.ini
.DS_Store

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Config/gripper_limits.yaml is generated by calibration but is tracked on
# purpose: it records the travel of the fingers currently fitted, and a clone
# without it cannot drive the gripper until it is calibrated afresh.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.log

progress.md
Data/

# Offline verification scripts — a working record of what was checked, not a
# committed test suite. See Verification/README.md.
Verification/
